  \"source_target\": \"repair:7.47-terminal finite-value algebraic clause; related corrected Theorem15.31 endpoint; not full B4 closure\",\n+  \"source_pages\": {\n+    \"pdf\": [\n+      141,\n+      142,\n+      278,\n+      279\n+    ],\n+    \"printed\": [\n+      129,\n+      130,\n+      266,\n+      267\n+    ]\n+  },\n+  \"source_pdf_sha256\": \"cef4edfa97a6e063e53e9c532717c50aa156e5bc782ea49f969b3385011a1b17\",\n+  \"header_sha256\": \"92e0dcfac53595e35b68bfd8083c09640d06da809355ab02ec4eb4b007b0bd67\",\n+  \"inputs\": {\n+    \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011/next-b4-readiness/v1.json\": \"4f9487f88840360b476bce2b7cff01748d414ba712e13baa9b785412effd1fcf\",\n+    \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011/next-b4-readiness/v1.md\": \"bce76c76d847bdaff8ce905d2b73713bc83d5b542377799cab2bd2ac6a8aee05\",\n+    \"BanditRLProof/OnlineWeightedPotential.lean\": \"63d94480e5e5a337acf5019c62e092fd36b1d2bf1a6edfc6f5b6bc5b95aa885a\",\n+    \"BanditRLProof/TsallisFTRLRegret.lean\": \"9a30a84e6dc0a20870aceb49826962c4ea783c09cf5262030a3d90f71966802f\",\n+    \"docs/contracts/online-ch2-complete-target-freeze-v1/effective-targets-frozen-v3.2.json\": \"61cf1901a632aeee35ee71511ba53b115ae0958649ea78b786536a4404684ba1\"\n+  },\n+  \"index_mapping\": {\n+    \"source t=1..T\": \"Lean t=0..T-1\",\n+    \"psi_source(t)\": \"psi (t-1)\",\n+    \"ell_source(t)\": \"loss (t-1)\",\n+    \"G_source(t)\": \"G (t-1), inclusive cumulative loss through range t\",\n+    \"x_source(t), real rounds\": \"y (t-1)=x (t-1), since t-1<T\",\n+    \"x_source(T+1)\": \"y T=z, arbitrary splice; no recurrence, optimizer, or producer premise\",\n+    \"regularizer_drift\": \"range (T-1) = source rounds1..T-1\",\n+    \"terminal_gap\": \"G (T-1) z-G (T-1) u retained with positive sign\"\n+  },\n+  \"assumptions\": [\n+    \"arbitrary state type E\",\n+    \"arbitrary real-valued regularizers/losses\",\n+    \"arbitrary trajectory x and comparator u and terminal z\",\n+    \"finite positive natural horizon T\"\n+  ],\n+  \"scope_boundary\": [\n+    \"No convexity, continuity, minimizer, hint, or algorithm assumptions\",\n+    \"Real-valued specialization only; EReal finiteness adapter remains separate mandatory debt\",\n+    \"No infinity totalization or source-invalid repaired endpoint acceptance\",\n+    \"T=0 excluded; T=1 empty drift and terminal gap retained\",\n+    \"All B1-B7 and remaining forward containers/future claims remain open\"\n+  ],\n+  \"reuse_decision\": \"TsallisFTRLRegret cumulativeLoss is generic sum, but its regret endpoints impose finite-action linear objectives and minimizer inequalities. No exact time-varying arbitrary-function equality reused as a black box. OnlineWeightedPotential exact signed identity has scalar separable weight structure; no forced dependency. Standard finite-sum telescoping is proposed substrate; no BODY constructed. Bounded retrieval receipts preserve search extent and failures.\",\n+  \"prospective_module\": \"BanditRLProof/OnlineCumulativePotential.lean (proposal only)\",\n+  \"public_api_count\": 1,\n+  \"definitions\": \"Only statement-local y and G lets; no new named public definitions. Neutral context consists entirely of imports and these exact lets.\",\n+  \"two_consumers\": [\n+    \"finite optimistic FTRL terminal-gap accounting\",\n+    \"finite corrected BTRL terminal accounting\"\n+  ],\n+  \"reader_delta\": \"One exact identity explanation with explicit source correction boundary, indexed drift and terminal gap; no container credit until full qualified producer/bound endpoints reviewed.\",\n+  \"graph_delta\": \"One prospective shared algebra node; actual TYPE/VALUE edges only after authorized proof/export; no teaching edge represented as proved implication.\",\n+  \"next_gates\": [\n+    \"parent leaf scope approval after current delivery\",\n+    \"fresh blind reconstruction from neutral header\",\n+    \"independent source/header review and freeze\",\n+    \"actual preproof context before any BODY\"\n+  ],\n+  \"decision_for_review\": \"The terminal is independently arbitrary via endpoint splice y T=z, preserving all real-round x values without a premise equating an arbitrary original x T to z. This semantic interface requires explicit source/header review.\"\n+}"},{"sha":"954be6d042250b3b5ff7baa0dadf4fd1c00aa9fa","filename":"runs/online-ch2-b4-finite-identity-20261011/header-proposal/header-proposal-v1.md","status":"added","additions":9,"deletions":0,"changes":9,"blob_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/blob/c445c93f7e4cda1408279d614858c904e346ad47/runs%2Fonline-ch2-b4-finite-identity-20261011%2Fheader-proposal%2Fheader-proposal-v1.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/raw/c445c93f7e4cda1408279d614858c904e346ad47/runs%2Fonline-ch2-b4-finite-identity-20261011%2Fheader-proposal%2Fheader-proposal-v1.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/contents/runs%2Fonline-ch2-b4-finite-identity-20261011%2Fheader-proposal%2Fheader-proposal-v1.md?ref=c445c93f7e4cda1408279d614858c904e346ad47","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@\n+# Finite cumulative-regret identity — proposal only\n+\n+One general algebraic leaf for `repair:7.47-terminal`; no theorem BODY or header elaboration performed. Source PDF141–142 and278–279 remain subject to the recorded terminal repairs. This is a finite-real specialization, not the full extended-value source theorem.\n+\n+The complete neutral header defines inclusive cumulative objectives G locally. Real source round t maps to Lean t−1. The endpoint splice y keeps every actual round x0,…,x(T−1), but sets yT=z independently. The equality retains both the signed regularizer drift and G(T−1,z)−G(T−1,u). T≥1 avoids a fictitious initial regularizer at zero horizon; T=1 has empty drift. No optimizer/convexity/producer or bound is assumed.\n+\n+Reuse searches are captured with exact argv, UTC, actual exits and full streams. Existing Tsallis linear/minimizer inequalities do not discharge this arbitrary-function equality; the accepted weighted identity has a different separable structure. Standard finite-sum algebra is the proposed substrate, without constructing a proof here. One proposed API serves future optimistic FTRL and corrected BTRL accounting; no duplicate selector or public helper chain is proposed.\n+\n+The intended reader delta is an exact indexed terminal-gap explanation. No source obligation/container is closed, no progress count is assigned, and all B1–B7 remain open. The splice interface, complete header and real-only boundary require fresh blind reconstruction and independent source review before freeze/BODY authorization. Prospective Lean/Overview/Functor changes describe one algebra node only; actual dependency edges await a proof and export."},{"sha":"e8c41afd9e2cdae2ad689ba829cbd59d40f9bfb5","filename":"runs/online-ch2-b4-finite-identity-20261011/header-proposal/manifest-v1.json","status":"added","additions":24,"deletions":0,"changes":24,"blob_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/blob/c445c93f7e4cda1408279d614858c904e346ad47/runs%2Fonline-ch2-b4-finite-identity-20261011%2Fheader-proposal%2Fmanifest-v1.json","raw_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/raw/c445c93f7e4cda1408279d614858c904e346ad47/runs%2Fonline-ch2-b4-finite-identity-20261011%2Fheader-proposal%2Fmanifest-v1.json","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/contents/runs%2Fonline-ch2-b4-finite-identity-20261011%2Fheader-proposal%2Fmanifest-v1.json?ref=c445c93f7e4cda1408279d614858c904e346ad47","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@\n+{\n+  \"scope\": \"Ignored proposal only; five retrieval commands actual exit0; no elaboration, BODY, browser, canonical changes or gates\",\n+  \"files\": {\n+    \"header-proposal-v1.json\": \"7a5848efbf57ba9c76c987baae75856331100325fc4c9130ead409b5ba3815fb\",\n+    \"header-proposal-v1.md\": \"b5ed53828138296c69e79870ab4a